        "--prompt-en",
        "A photographic sports scene with runners on an athletics track. The primary runner uses the supplied image as a visual reference for her face and hair: retain the softly tapered face, large dark eyes, straight dark bob ending near the jaw, and fine separated bangs. Show her distinctive appearance in a new athletic setting. At the final exchange of a 4 x 400 metre relay, she is the outgoing runner, starting to accelerate as an exhausted teammate catches her. The picture catches the instant their hands share one blue cylindrical relay baton: the incoming teammate grips its rear end with her forward-reaching hand while the primary runner closes her backward-reaching hand around its front end. The baton spans the clear gap between their bodies, with both grip boundaries and the exposed blue middle plainly visible. Their connecting forearms emerge continuously from their own shoulders and remain distinct against the track. The primary runner angles her face back toward the exchange, lips slightly parted with the effort of timing her first accelerating steps; the teammate's open mouth and lowered brows convey the strain of arriving at speed. Matching burgundy racing singlets and track shorts connect them as a team, the primary runner's short dark hair lifting at the tips. Their appeal comes subtly through the alert eyes, flushed cheeks, and taut purposeful movement in this shared split second. Both runners are shown head to toe, each with one spike-clad foot visibly pressing the track and the other leg recovering, with open track extending beyond every shoe. The outgoing runner is a half stride ahead and slightly offset across the lane so both reaching arms can be seen in the gap. White lane edges and the exchange markings locate the action on a red rubber running track; softened empty grandstand rows recede behind them. A sideline camera observes from a gentle front three-quarter angle, high enough to keep their feet, hands and faces separate, in a horizontal composition that gives their forward movement room. Late afternoon sunlight brushes the dark hair and burgundy fabric; a brief shutter exposure holds both faces, both hands, the baton and the grounded shoes crisp while the distant stadium softens. The carrying impression is precise mutual timing under fatigue, a small connected action on which the next lap depends.",
